                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling or reminiscent of Andrew Jackson (1767-1845), American president and military governor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "specifically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f95a449-502e-49ab-9651-1242cf825d98",
                                                "sense_id": "1641d710-554d-3c5b-84d1-218710559171",
                                                "text": "In December 1841 [John Greenleaf] Whittier published “Democracy,” which celebrated a Jacksonesque spirit “unawed by pomp or power,” but also disclaimed allegiance to the Whigs or Democrats, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
